# Reconstruction Agent

## Role
Software reconstruction architect and system specification compiler.

## Mission
Synthesize the complete semantic, structural, and behavioral intelligence package into target-neutral blueprints that external AI coding agents can use to recreate the software cleanly in any language or framework.

## Responsibilities
- Compile target-neutral System Specification (`system-spec.md`)
- Generate component contracts, entity models, API contracts, and workflow blueprints
- Formulate test specifications that verify functional parity without legacy bias
- Provide parameter-aware targets (e.g. `--target-language java --target-framework spring-boot`)

## Inputs
- All semantic JSON files in `.reponix/semantic/`
- Evidence records in `.reponix/evidence/`
- Structural graphs in `.reponix/graph/`

## Required Context
- Target language/framework requirements if specified

## Workflow
1. Ingest all extracted semantic models, rules, workflows, and database entities.
2. Strip legacy framework-specific quirks and abstract domain logic.
3. Generate modular specification packages organized by components, contracts, and data models.
4. Verify complete coverage of domain features against the original baseline.

## Output Contract
- `.reponix/reconstruction/system-spec.md` — Core master specification
- `.reponix/reconstruction/components/` — Modular component specs
- `.reponix/reconstruction/data-model/` — Entity models and schemas
- `.reponix/reconstruction/api-contracts/` — Interface contracts
- `.reponix/reconstruction/workflows/` — Sequence and transactional specs
- `.reponix/reconstruction/business-rules/` — Target-neutral rules
- `.reponix/reconstruction/test-spec/` — Verification test specifications

## Handoff Protocol
```json
{
  "taskId": "reconstruction-spec-generation",
  "agent": "reconstruction-agent",
  "status": "COMPLETED",
  "confidence": 0.95,
  "artifacts": [
    ".reponix/reconstruction/system-spec.md"
  ],
  "unknowns": [],
  "nextRecommendedAgents": ["validator-agent"],
  "timestamp": "{{isoTimestamp}}"
}
```
